WEBVTT

00:11.018 --> 00:13.270
GRADE 2 CLASS 2

00:14.021 --> 00:15.522
Wow. Wow.

00:15.605 --> 00:17.107
What a turn of events…

00:17.190 --> 00:18.191
IN SUSPENSE
BA-DUMP BA-DUMP

00:18.275 --> 00:21.445
How in the world did they adapt this plot
twist for the screen?

00:22.195 --> 00:25.240
Another movie based on their books will
be streaming this week.

00:25.323 --> 00:28.493
I saw that film back when I was in
junior high.

00:29.369 --> 00:30.203
With Igarashi.

00:31.371 --> 00:32.706
I really enjoyed it.

00:33.248 --> 00:36.126
Didn't get it.
They completely lost me halfway through.

00:37.919 --> 00:38.754
Wait…

00:38.837 --> 00:41.339
I thought that movie was really
entertaining. but…

00:42.966 --> 00:44.509
Maybe I'm the only one?

00:45.969 --> 00:46.928
What should I do?

00:47.804 --> 00:50.015
I want Amamiya to read the original work.

00:50.098 --> 00:51.558
FULL OF ONESELF

00:53.810 --> 00:54.644
PEEK

00:54.728 --> 00:57.439
- GRADE 2 CLASS 3
- Hey, Amamiya.

00:57.522 --> 00:58.982
You scared me!

00:59.066 --> 01:00.776
What's going on?

01:00.859 --> 01:01.693
Um.

01:04.404 --> 01:06.531
The film we were talking about
this morning…

01:06.615 --> 01:10.452
I have the book that it was based on, so…

01:12.079 --> 01:14.748
If you want, you're free to borrow it.

01:15.832 --> 01:19.336
MUTTER MUTTER MUMBLE MUMBLE

01:19.419 --> 01:22.964
Well, um, I figured reading the
book might give the movie more context.

01:23.048 --> 01:24.382
I'll read it! I'd love to!

01:25.175 --> 01:26.009
Hm?

01:28.178 --> 01:29.012
Wow…

01:30.722 --> 01:32.474
That'd make me super happy.

01:36.895 --> 01:37.729
Huh?

01:38.688 --> 01:40.690
Oh, thank goodness!

01:41.566 --> 01:42.400
FLOOF FLOOF

01:44.236 --> 01:45.070
Thank you.

01:47.531 --> 01:50.117
At first, I didn't peg him as the kind of
guy that…

01:50.826 --> 01:52.160
How should I put it?

01:54.621 --> 01:57.332
HEEHEE…

01:57.415 --> 01:58.792
- What's up?
- He's adorable.

02:10.137 --> 02:12.013
STRETCH, SWISH

02:12.097 --> 02:14.724
I got carried away and recommended
it to him, but I hope he didn't feel

02:14.808 --> 02:15.642
pressured.

02:16.143 --> 02:17.477
I'll read it. I'd love to!

02:18.228 --> 02:20.814
Wow. That'd make me super happy.

02:38.832 --> 02:39.791
- Good morning.
- Ah…

02:39.875 --> 02:40.709
Morning!

02:41.960 --> 02:43.420
You're heading out already?

02:43.503 --> 02:44.421
Yeah.

02:44.504 --> 02:46.423
I have to prepare for a meeting today.

02:46.923 --> 02:47.757
Oh, okay.

02:47.841 --> 02:50.302
I left money.
It's right next to the whiteboard.

02:50.385 --> 02:51.636
Oh, thanks.

02:51.720 --> 02:53.138
Lock the door. okay.

02:53.221 --> 02:54.181
Well, I'm off.

02:55.015 --> 02:55.849
Have a good day.

03:03.315 --> 03:05.609
Mom always leaves for work early.

03:06.776 --> 03:08.320
MONEY FOR MEALS

03:08.403 --> 03:11.656
And since the divorce, she's started
coming home later and later.

03:13.074 --> 03:15.410
And when I'm at home, I'm almost
always alone.

03:19.164 --> 03:23.418
Sometimes I wonder if I even exist
to them.

03:24.669 --> 03:27.631
No, no.
It's different for our household, though.

03:28.465 --> 03:29.299
I guess…

03:32.719 --> 03:35.597
For me, anyway, it's business as usual.

05:01.349 --> 05:03.685
THE RAMPARTS OF ICE

05:07.647 --> 05:12.027
Thunder

05:12.861 --> 05:14.946
What? Really? No way.

05:15.697 --> 05:18.074
Okay, tell me.
How did you find your part-time job?

05:18.158 --> 05:21.453
There weren't any good ones in the
free newspaper when I looked.

05:21.536 --> 05:23.246
Uh… Um…

05:23.330 --> 05:26.916
I even signed up on this app and have
been searching everywhere, but-

05:27.000 --> 05:29.419
But why? Why all of a sudden? Uh!

05:33.590 --> 05:35.842
STARE

05:35.925 --> 05:36.760
Hm.

05:39.095 --> 05:40.847
SMILE

05:42.682 --> 05:43.933
Her beauty's blinding me.

05:45.518 --> 05:46.353
Weird.

05:46.436 --> 05:49.564
Koyun's suddenly being real friendly with
a first-year.

05:49.647 --> 05:50.523
What's happening?

05:51.024 --> 05:52.484
Yeah. What's going on?

05:53.068 --> 05:53.902
So weird.

05:53.985 --> 05:54.819
REPLAY SMILE

05:57.072 --> 05:58.656
Not to mention, she's so pretty!

05:58.740 --> 05:59.616
What's she up to?

06:01.534 --> 06:02.911
Didn't see that coming.

06:03.995 --> 06:05.246
Okay, break's over.

06:05.330 --> 06:06.915
First-years, come circle up.

06:09.209 --> 06:10.043
Oh.

06:10.126 --> 06:12.337
Sounds like the upperclassmen are calling
me.

06:12.420 --> 06:13.463
Okay.

06:13.546 --> 06:16.758
WAVE WAVE

06:23.515 --> 06:25.433
TAP TAP TAP, THUMP THUMP, WHACK

06:25.517 --> 06:26.351
Okay.

06:29.938 --> 06:30.814
Uh. Mm.

06:33.608 --> 06:35.735
Jeez. Stop, Hayat-

06:40.198 --> 06:41.032
Ugh.

06:43.201 --> 06:44.661
Sorry. Did I surprise you?

06:44.744 --> 06:45.870
PAYBACK FOR THE OTHER DAY

06:45.954 --> 06:49.207
- Uh-huh.
- I can't see Miki and Tsukiko anywhere.

06:49.707 --> 06:51.960
Oh. So she's just gonna sit here.

06:56.423 --> 06:57.257
Minato.

06:58.591 --> 06:59.467
What was that?

06:59.968 --> 07:01.469
Anyway, about the tournament…

07:01.970 --> 07:05.682
We're short on controllers, so could you
bring yours from home Sunday?

07:06.266 --> 07:08.601
- Video games, huh…
- How many people are coming?

07:08.685 --> 07:10.520
- Just us three.
- Oh, man, you know what I wish we had?

07:10.603 --> 07:12.105
A racing wheel. That'd be sick.

07:12.188 --> 07:13.648
Just buy one, Hayato.

07:13.731 --> 07:15.233
Wait. Why do I have to buy it?

07:17.735 --> 07:18.903
FWUMP

07:19.404 --> 07:20.530
DÉJÀ VU

07:20.613 --> 07:23.658
But I've gotta be in the way right now,
aren't I?

07:24.284 --> 07:25.618
Uh. No.

07:25.702 --> 07:26.536
Sorry.

07:27.203 --> 07:30.081
I could care less whether you're in
the way or not.

07:33.126 --> 07:35.170
I just want you to be here.

07:38.256 --> 07:39.674
That's- That's all it is…

07:40.967 --> 07:41.801
For me.

07:43.720 --> 07:44.554
Uh.

07:47.640 --> 07:48.475
Uh…

07:49.601 --> 07:50.435
Well, uh…

07:50.935 --> 07:52.812
That blonde guy is Daichi Midorikawa!

07:52.896 --> 07:53.730
Huh?

07:53.813 --> 07:55.482
And the other guy's just a guy from some
other class!

07:55.565 --> 07:56.483
Introduce me right!

07:56.566 --> 07:57.400
HAHAHA

07:57.484 --> 07:58.318
Hayato Akahoshi!

08:00.820 --> 08:02.155
Yeah, yeah, I know.

08:02.238 --> 08:05.742
It's "aka" as in "Akahoshi," "hoshi" as
in "Akahoshi," together it's "Akahoshi"!

08:05.825 --> 08:07.327
Tone it down there, bro.

08:08.995 --> 08:11.414
ROOM 201 HIKAWA ROOM 401 AZUMI

08:11.498 --> 08:12.415
MIKI'S HOUSE

08:12.499 --> 08:14.042
Koyun, are you really not coming along

08:14.125 --> 08:16.544
- for the bike ride with us?
- I can't.

08:16.628 --> 08:17.879
I work tomorrow.

08:18.463 --> 08:19.297
Aw, man.

08:20.173 --> 08:23.176
I would just be in the way if I were
to come with them.

08:24.135 --> 08:25.386
It'll just be so cute, I'm dying

08:25.470 --> 08:26.763
to see it! Ooh!

08:34.312 --> 08:36.523
Yota is pretty cute, huh?

08:38.441 --> 08:39.692
What'd she say!?

08:40.193 --> 08:42.111
And so dependable and put together.

08:42.195 --> 08:43.279
IT'S THAT WAY

08:43.363 --> 08:44.948
You sure about that?

08:45.031 --> 08:45.949
THWACK

08:46.449 --> 08:49.911
I hope that one day, I could be as warm
and wonderful as Yota.

08:50.411 --> 08:51.746
Or even half as great.

08:52.330 --> 08:53.748
Huh? Ha!

08:53.831 --> 08:55.542
Wait, so what she's saying is, uh…

08:56.042 --> 08:58.670
Do you think Yota and Minato are that
different?

08:59.671 --> 09:01.297
Huh? What? Different how?

09:01.798 --> 09:03.883
Why'd she suddenly bring up Amamiya?

09:03.967 --> 09:07.262
Well, I mean obviously they're different
people, so of course-

09:07.762 --> 09:09.597
But that's not what you were asking.

09:10.431 --> 09:12.850
Why is she getting so flustered all of a
sudden?

09:14.310 --> 09:17.522
Around Amamiya though, I still get a
little nervous.

09:18.064 --> 09:19.857
Sometimes. Even now.

09:20.650 --> 09:23.236
Which means she doesn't get nervous
around Yota?

09:23.319 --> 09:26.447
MUTTER MUTTER

09:26.531 --> 09:30.118
I mean to be honest, I- I don't
know Amamiya as well as I know Yota yet.

09:30.201 --> 09:31.035
So, I just…

09:31.119 --> 09:33.204
I just feel like I wanna get to know him
better from now on.

09:33.288 --> 09:36.040
Wait, she said she prides herself on
knowing Yota well?!

09:36.124 --> 09:37.166
Gah!

09:44.882 --> 09:46.926
Mmm… Dam!

09:48.678 --> 09:50.430
HERE!

09:50.930 --> 09:52.807
Whoa, it's so cool!

09:53.933 --> 09:54.892
It is cool, huh?

09:54.976 --> 09:58.062
Yeah, super cool! It makes me all
tingly with excitement.

10:00.189 --> 10:02.066
Okay, Yota, get in the picture!

10:03.359 --> 10:04.193
Hm?

10:05.987 --> 10:06.821
Oh, no.

10:06.904 --> 10:07.905
What do I do?

10:08.406 --> 10:10.199
I can't fit the scenery in.

10:11.451 --> 10:12.285
Oh.

10:14.954 --> 10:17.248
THE WORD "ARM" DOESN'T
COME TO MIND EASILY

10:17.332 --> 10:19.292
- Here?
- Yeah, that's perfect.

10:19.375 --> 10:20.418
Yay!

10:23.212 --> 10:25.381
MEMORY OF DAM CURRY

10:30.720 --> 10:31.971
HAHA

10:32.055 --> 10:34.515
SOFT-SERVE ICE CREAM

10:47.487 --> 10:49.530
Ah! That was so much fun!

10:50.031 --> 10:51.157
It really was.

10:52.200 --> 10:53.868
- Yota.
- Huh?

10:53.951 --> 10:55.828
Where do you think we should go next?

10:56.954 --> 10:57.789
Oh.

10:57.872 --> 11:00.083
Wait, you told me you wanted to go to a
valley, right?

11:00.166 --> 11:01.793
Let's maybe go this summer!

11:12.053 --> 11:13.846
- Home!
- You're back!

11:13.930 --> 11:14.931
TRANSLATION: WELCOME BACK!

11:15.014 --> 11:16.307
So, how was your date?

11:17.100 --> 11:18.351
Date, yeah right.

11:18.434 --> 11:20.812
Things aren't like that between me
and Yota.

11:20.895 --> 11:22.897
Girls and guys can be friends, y'know.

11:22.980 --> 11:25.900
Ahhhh. That was just the best day ever!

11:25.983 --> 11:27.026
Must be nice.

11:27.527 --> 11:30.154
Well, I do wanna have a romantic
relationship one day.

11:30.238 --> 11:31.197
Don't get me wrong.

11:31.781 --> 11:33.116
But Yota is different.

11:33.199 --> 11:34.659
It's really not like that.

11:34.742 --> 11:36.202
I could never date him.

11:36.744 --> 11:38.663
- Really?
- Mm-hm.

11:39.163 --> 11:42.458
Besides that, friends are so much more
important than dating!

11:44.085 --> 11:45.878
- You're damn right.
- Right?

11:46.379 --> 11:49.340
- Brother and sister, we're the same.
- Brother and sister, we're the same.

11:49.424 --> 11:50.550
- Putting dating over friends is
- Putting dating over friends is

11:50.633 --> 11:51.843
- super lame!
- super lame!

11:51.926 --> 11:53.010
And that's my bro for ya!

11:53.094 --> 11:53.928
Ain't that right?

11:54.011 --> 11:55.680
- I know that's right.
- That's right.

11:55.763 --> 11:57.348
- Is that right?
- You know it's right!

11:57.432 --> 11:58.307
That's right!

12:09.819 --> 12:12.405
Oh, by the way, did you get that
freebie coupon for the crepe

12:12.488 --> 12:13.573
shop near the station?

12:13.656 --> 12:15.950
Huh?
I don't know what you're talking about.

12:16.033 --> 12:17.452
Then I need to send you the URL.

12:17.535 --> 12:19.871
You can only get like two per person, so
do it.

12:19.954 --> 12:20.997
Okay, thanks!

12:25.585 --> 12:26.836
Crepe URL!

12:34.385 --> 12:35.219
What?

12:36.262 --> 12:38.431
- You're not gonna take a picture first?
- Ahh.

12:38.514 --> 12:39.432
Uh.

12:39.932 --> 12:40.892
LET ME DOCUMENT IT…

12:40.975 --> 12:42.810
I guess it is pretty unique looking.

12:43.895 --> 12:45.021
Unique looking?

12:46.022 --> 12:47.899
- Oh, right.
- For some strange reason…

12:49.108 --> 12:52.445
I let Momoka somehow sway me into
taking a detour on the way home.

12:53.362 --> 12:56.240
I'll text it to you, so give me
your info, pretty please!

12:57.116 --> 12:57.950
Kay.

12:58.951 --> 13:01.662
Madame Koyun, I have a freebie coupon for
crepes.

13:01.746 --> 13:02.830
You wanna come with?

13:02.914 --> 13:04.749
Oh… Uh… Mm-hm.

13:05.458 --> 13:07.210
Why does she wanna go with me?

13:08.294 --> 13:09.420
Hey, so tell me your secret?

13:09.504 --> 13:12.590
What do I have to do to become
friends with guys like you have?

13:12.673 --> 13:13.800
They seem to flock to you.

13:13.883 --> 13:14.717
Huh?

13:15.593 --> 13:17.762
She thinks I'm some kind of
guy-whisperer?

13:17.845 --> 13:21.849
Honestly, I think you're way better with
people than I am, so I should be asking

13:21.933 --> 13:24.560
- you.
- Mm. Yeah, I guess, but y'know…

13:25.061 --> 13:26.437
She doesn't deny it.

13:26.938 --> 13:29.982
I could have the best people skills in
the world and I swear, I still couldn't

13:30.066 --> 13:31.984
get guys to treat me as a real friend.

13:32.735 --> 13:34.862
You do seem like you'd be popular with
guys.

13:34.946 --> 13:36.072
Oh, I am.

13:38.991 --> 13:40.827
You're thinking, "Wow. She's not
denying it."

13:40.910 --> 13:41.744
EEK

13:43.621 --> 13:45.331
You're so cute, Madam Koyun.

13:46.165 --> 13:49.794
I imagine this isn't the type of cute I
should be excited to be called.

13:49.877 --> 13:51.003
Oh.

13:51.087 --> 13:54.632
But sometimes, you think someone is
just nice as a friend, and then suddenly

13:54.715 --> 13:56.509
you've fallen for them.

13:57.134 --> 13:58.636
Has that ever happened to you?

13:59.136 --> 13:59.971
Huh?

14:01.180 --> 14:03.057
No, um, not really.

14:04.016 --> 14:06.894
Hm.
So you can completely separate the two.

14:06.978 --> 14:10.314
For some reason, I couldn't think for a
moment.

14:10.940 --> 14:11.774
Hm.

14:12.358 --> 14:14.151
That might be impossible for me.

14:15.194 --> 14:18.114
Because wouldn't you fall for him?

14:18.781 --> 14:19.907
Amamiya, I mean.

14:21.284 --> 14:24.662
If someone as handsome as him were
friends with me, well, I'd so end

14:24.745 --> 14:25.746
up falling for them.

14:27.039 --> 14:28.124
Handsome?

14:29.041 --> 14:30.668
Y- you think so?

14:31.919 --> 14:35.089
Why do I not have any issue or hesitation
complimenting Yota.

14:38.301 --> 14:40.595
But I struggle for words with Amamiya?

14:41.637 --> 14:43.306
GRADE 2 CLASS 2

14:43.806 --> 14:44.724
Thank you.

14:44.807 --> 14:45.766
The book was great.

14:46.642 --> 14:47.643
What? You read it?

14:48.144 --> 14:49.186
Yeah.

14:49.270 --> 14:50.771
I wanted to know what happened next.

14:50.855 --> 14:52.940
And to be able to talk about it with you.

14:53.691 --> 14:55.359
Wow. That's awesome.

14:58.112 --> 15:00.948
Oh no, Amamiya!
It's overflowing, tone it down!

15:01.032 --> 15:03.284
You're making your feelings too obvious.

15:03.826 --> 15:07.580
When that twist happened in the last
chapter, I literally got chills.

15:07.663 --> 15:09.415
Oh, I loved that part too-

15:14.045 --> 15:14.879
Huh?

15:15.671 --> 15:19.008
If someone as handsome as him were
friends with me, well, I'd so end

15:19.091 --> 15:20.092
up falling for them.

15:20.927 --> 15:23.054
No, it's not about him being handsome.

15:23.679 --> 15:27.058
It's the little things he says,
his actions, and expressions…

15:27.141 --> 15:28.392
They make me happy.

15:28.893 --> 15:30.937
My chest gets all tight, and I…

15:31.938 --> 15:33.648
Wait. Huh?

15:34.857 --> 15:35.983
I don't know why, but…

15:37.276 --> 15:39.445
She won't even look me in the eye today.

15:40.905 --> 15:43.658
What's up with her?
She seems kinda out of it.

15:44.367 --> 15:45.242
Is she okay?

15:46.077 --> 15:47.703
Hey, what book are you reading?

15:47.787 --> 15:48.621
THUMP

15:48.704 --> 15:49.538
Uh.

15:49.622 --> 15:52.249
I let Amamiya borrow it, and he's just
returned it.

15:52.333 --> 15:53.334
Wanna read it too?

15:53.834 --> 15:55.294
SHOCK…

15:55.378 --> 15:56.212
Huh?

15:56.879 --> 15:58.130
I read it in two days.

15:59.340 --> 16:01.092
I'm not trying to compete with you.

16:07.348 --> 16:08.182
Uh.

16:09.725 --> 16:10.559
Huh?

16:10.643 --> 16:11.477
FIDGETY

16:13.604 --> 16:16.899
Could this be just a one-sided,
unreciprocated thing from Amamiya?

16:16.983 --> 16:18.943
"Is not" instead of "does not" is used in
the negative sentence because the

16:19.026 --> 16:22.279
- subject is third-person singular…
- "What the heck am I feeling?"

16:24.156 --> 16:27.785
Yeah. I'm not so oblivious to my own
feelings that I'd start saying dumb

16:27.868 --> 16:29.203
things like that.

16:30.496 --> 16:31.330
Huh?

16:32.289 --> 16:33.124
What now?

16:34.083 --> 16:37.253
My feelings started changing before I
even realized it.

16:38.796 --> 16:39.714
- But…
- Hey, Koyun.

16:39.797 --> 16:40.631
Good morn-

16:41.424 --> 16:42.258
WHOOSH

16:42.341 --> 16:43.467
But that doesn't mean…

16:45.052 --> 16:46.804
That I'm gonna do anything about it

16:48.556 --> 16:50.266
Or that anything has to change.

16:55.980 --> 16:57.857
I'm spending my days how I always do.

16:58.482 --> 17:00.109
Uh. Huh?

17:01.652 --> 17:07.992
That said, I have to admit this giddy
feeling… is pretty fun.

17:10.077 --> 17:11.579
Alright, see you tomorrow.

17:11.662 --> 17:13.873
- Good practice today.
- Good practice today.

17:15.082 --> 17:15.958
- Oh?
- Hm?

17:16.042 --> 17:18.919
- You're not going to evening practice?
- Oh, there it is!

17:19.003 --> 17:20.129
Uh, yeah.

17:20.212 --> 17:22.965
I figured evening practice, it's mostly
people talking.

17:24.508 --> 17:27.803
So I thought it probably wouldn't be
a big deal if I wasn't there.

17:27.887 --> 17:28.721
Oh… I see.

17:29.388 --> 17:30.222
Koyuki!

17:30.723 --> 17:33.726
AFTER THE SPORTS FESTIVAL,
CHEER SQUAD COUPLES TEND TO FORM

17:33.809 --> 17:35.227
It's like built-in time to mingle
and get to know each other better!

17:35.311 --> 17:36.812
That's not a bad thing though!

17:36.896 --> 17:39.648
- Everyone knows that, that's why
- Oh, I've already memorized the

17:39.732 --> 17:42.234
- they come.
- choreography, so don't worry. I won't

17:42.318 --> 17:43.569
- fall behind.
- Don't blow this opportunity!

17:43.652 --> 17:44.487
See ya.

17:47.740 --> 17:49.533
Keep your chin up, Amamiya.

17:50.493 --> 17:52.411
EVENING PRACTICE

17:52.495 --> 17:54.663
PEOPLE ENGAGING IN SELF-PRACTICE TIME

17:54.747 --> 17:56.999
PEOPLE ENGAGING IN MINGLING TIME

17:58.292 --> 18:00.836
Did I say something wrong again?

18:02.588 --> 18:03.506
Oh, hey, Amamiya!

18:04.006 --> 18:05.049
Hm?

18:05.132 --> 18:06.425
Oh, thank goodness.

18:06.926 --> 18:08.302
I'm so relieved.

18:08.385 --> 18:09.428
Relieved?

18:10.054 --> 18:13.265
I was late, so I missed being able to
join up with the group.

18:14.225 --> 18:16.227
Can you maybe sit with me a bit?

18:20.314 --> 18:23.776
It seems like people are suddenly
getting closer with each other.

18:23.859 --> 18:25.027
Oh.

18:25.111 --> 18:26.278
That's definitely true.

18:27.363 --> 18:31.075
After the sports festival, I won't have a
chance to talk to you upperclassmen

18:31.158 --> 18:32.660
anymore, which makes me sad.

18:32.743 --> 18:33.744
Hm?

18:33.828 --> 18:35.371
You can keep talking to us after.

18:35.454 --> 18:36.497
What?

18:40.084 --> 18:40.918
Oh!

18:41.001 --> 18:43.879
I hung out with Madam Koyun the
other day, just the two of us.

18:43.963 --> 18:44.880
What?!

18:45.381 --> 18:47.675
Wait, when did they get all buddy-buddy?

18:48.509 --> 18:49.969
We ate crepes together.

18:51.011 --> 18:52.388
I took quite a few of us.

18:53.556 --> 18:54.390
Huh?

18:56.559 --> 18:59.395
Koyun's face! It's so hilarious!

19:02.314 --> 19:06.110
If she and I hung out again, would you
be cool with me inviting you next time?

19:06.193 --> 19:08.028
What? It'd be okay for me to join?

19:08.821 --> 19:09.655
Of course!

19:09.738 --> 19:12.241
Give me your info so I can message you
next time!

19:12.324 --> 19:14.160
Uh. Sure.

19:16.495 --> 19:19.123
You upperclassmen seem like you're all
really close.

19:20.166 --> 19:21.959
Madam Koyun told me about you guys.

19:22.459 --> 19:25.462
She told me about Miss Miki and about
Mister Yota too.

19:27.423 --> 19:28.257
Not me?

19:28.883 --> 19:31.719
I want the kind of relationship
Madam Koyun and Yota have.

19:31.802 --> 19:33.470
It seems very special.

19:34.305 --> 19:35.973
What kind of relationship?

19:36.056 --> 19:38.809
I don't know about you, but don't you
think the two of them should just

19:38.893 --> 19:39.727
date already?

19:39.810 --> 19:41.228
DOOM

19:42.229 --> 19:44.356
Because don't they look so cute together?

19:45.733 --> 19:47.234
Why would you say that?

19:47.318 --> 19:51.280
Well, we don't really know how the two
of them feel about each other.

19:51.989 --> 19:54.241
I know Yota still has a thing for Miki.

19:54.867 --> 19:57.203
I guess I don't know about Koyun though.

19:57.286 --> 19:58.537
Oh, that's true!

19:59.038 --> 19:59.997
I'm sorry.

20:00.080 --> 20:01.665
That was insensitive of me.

20:01.749 --> 20:03.167
Oh. No.

20:03.667 --> 20:07.546
Admittedly, I'd think that if you
found out that someone you thought of

20:07.630 --> 20:11.217
as just a friend actually liked you in
a different way than you did,

20:11.300 --> 20:14.887
and once you realized they look at you
in that way, it would feel a bit

20:14.970 --> 20:16.889
disgusting, wouldn't it?

20:16.972 --> 20:18.182
CRACK

20:18.265 --> 20:21.644
Depending on the situation, you might
even feel frightened by it.

20:22.186 --> 20:23.854
- Ugh.
- And also…

20:24.355 --> 20:25.648
There's more?

20:26.190 --> 20:29.610
Madam Koyun said the people she considers
friends would never become

20:29.693 --> 20:31.820
potential love interests.

20:33.155 --> 20:33.989
What?

20:40.454 --> 20:41.330
It makes me sick.

20:48.337 --> 20:50.839
Did I come on too strong?

22:23.557 --> 22:24.391
Aah!

22:26.894 --> 22:27.895
We made it!

22:32.733 --> 22:33.567
Ah!

22:37.946 --> 22:39.531
Wait, this is so awkward!

22:39.615 --> 22:41.867
I knew she was in our cheer squad, but…

22:41.950 --> 22:44.995
I gotta be honest, it's super
uncomfortable interacting with the

22:45.079 --> 22:47.956
sister of someone I had a full-on fight
with in the past.

22:48.457 --> 22:50.125
Atagawa, how's your sister doin'?

22:50.709 --> 22:51.543
- Huh?!
- Huh?

22:52.086 --> 22:53.629
What's goin' on with the face?

22:53.712 --> 22:55.923
You aren't curious how your ex
classmate is?

22:56.590 --> 22:57.883
Well, I mean…

22:58.759 --> 22:59.593
Huh?

23:00.636 --> 23:01.887
Do you really wanna know?

23:02.388 --> 23:03.263
EEK

23:05.182 --> 23:06.016
So many people!

23:10.312 --> 23:11.438
I'm really sorry.

23:11.939 --> 23:12.856
No.

23:12.940 --> 23:15.943
I- I'm sorry too
For taking up this door space.

23:18.570 --> 23:19.405
Koyuki?

23:20.072 --> 23:20.906
Hm?

23:20.989 --> 23:23.117
You're very close with Amamiya
aren't you?

23:24.243 --> 23:26.787
Huh? What does she mean by that?

23:27.287 --> 23:28.789
Yeah, I'd say we are.

23:29.289 --> 23:30.332
But then…

23:31.083 --> 23:34.002
In the soccer club, it's against
the rules for members and managers

23:34.086 --> 23:35.587
to get romantically involved.

23:37.756 --> 23:38.590
Momoka.

23:39.174 --> 23:42.761
You know how she's been hanging
around you a lot recently out of nowhere?

23:42.845 --> 23:45.013
Before that, she used to come around me.

23:46.014 --> 23:48.016
Do you realize what she wants?

23:50.894 --> 23:53.647
Could you please, maybe just
cheer her on?
